This repository ("compile-time-browser" / ctbrowser) is a derivative
work built on:

    compile-time-javascript (ctjs)  https://github.com/alexios-angel/compile-time-javascript
    compile-time-css   (ctcss)  https://github.com/alexios-angel/compile-time-css

each of which is built on:

    notre (a fork of Compile Time Regular Expressions)
    https://github.com/alexios-angel/notre

which is itself a derivative of:

    Compile Time Regular Expressions (CTRE)
    https://github.com/hanickadot/compile-time-regular-expressions
    Copyright (c) Hana Dusikova and the CTRE contributors

License: Apache License 2.0, with LLVM Exceptions (see LICENSE in this
repository, reproduced unmodified from upstream).

What is derived
---------------
The two remaining bricks arrive as git submodules under external/ and
carry their own NOTICE files (historical CTLL/CTRE lineage, the
ECMA-262 and W3C CSS semantics; compile-time-containers, MIT, supplies
the constexpr containers). This repository began as a clone of
compile-time-css - the chain runs compile-time-xml ->
compile-time-html -> compile-time-css -> here - and keeps that git
history. The DOM (its own WHATWG tokenizer and tree builder), the
style, layout, paint and raster pipeline, the script VM and standard
library, and the SDL3 shell are original to this repository.

The vendored fonts/ directory carries Tinos, Fira Sans and Cousine
from the Google Fonts collection (github.com/google/fonts), each
licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 - see fonts/README.md
and the OFL texts there. They are loaded through the asset registry as
the default serif/sans-serif/monospace faces.

Attribution for the historical CTLL engine belongs to Hana Dusikova;
this file preserves it as required by Section 4(c) of the Apache
License 2.0 for the versions that shipped it.

The embedded 8x8 bitmap font (src/raster/font8x8.hpp) is
PUBLIC DOMAIN: font8x8 by Daniel Hepper <daniel@hepper.net>
(https://github.com/dhepper/font8x8), based on public-domain work by
Marcel Sondaar / International Business Machines.

The example assets (examples/assets/) are generated deterministically
by tools/gen-assets.py in this repository and carry no third-party
